=begin pod

=head1 Using the Config mode

The 'config' mode is designed for complex projects as exemplified in
the directory 'example-projects/israel-trip/'.

=head2 'config' file options when present in the file

=head3 C<=ofile Str>

Output file name of the new document

=head3 C<=numbers Bool>

Explicit 'true' or 'false' OR, with no value: True if present, False
if not

Produces page numbers on each page except the cover which is number
'i' (one but not shown); format: 'Page N of M' (a title page by
default gets a blank reverse page which is page 'ii' but is not shown)

=head3 C<=begin title>

Empty or no title block: no cover page


title line for the cover page

# a retained blank line for the cover page

another title line for the cover page

=head3 C<=end title>

=head3 C<=two-sided Bool>

Explicit 'true' or 'false' OR, with no value: True if present, False
if not

=head3 C<=back Bool>

Explicit 'true' or 'false' OR, with no value: True if present, False
if not

=head3 C<=paper size-type>

'Letter' or 'A4' [default: Letter]

=head3 C<=margins Numeric>

Size in PostScript points [default: 72 (one inch)]

=head3 C<=compress Numeric?>

empty OR 150 or 300 [default: empty (none)]

Numberic is the dots per inch (dpi) value

=end pod
